## 2. Page Inventory

Every page this feature touches. Verified against the existing frontend scaffold: the application currently contains a single `/` route rendering inline content (no header, no layout, no settings page, no dashboard, no resource pages).

### P-F022-001 — Root / Home
**Type:** Existing (modified)
**Path:** /
**Purpose:** Existing bootstrap landing page; content unchanged; now rendered inside the new application layout so the header notification indicator is visible platform-wide.
**Permission gate:** None (anonymous reachable; indicator hidden for anonymous users)
**Feature source:** US-F022-001, FR-F022-004 (header indicator surface)

### P-F022-002 — Notification Center
**Type:** New
**Path:** /notifications
**Purpose:** Lists the identified user's system-generated notifications (title, message, timestamp, read state), newest first, with server-side pagination; provides per-row mark-as-read and mark-all-as-read; provides a link to Notification Preferences.
**Permission gate:** Authenticated session (TD §17 — DRF `IsAuthenticated` default; anonymous → 401)
**Feature source:** US-F022-002, US-F022-003, FR-F022-001..007, AC-F022-001..005

### P-F022-003 — Notification Preferences
**Type:** New
**Path:** /notifications/preferences
**Purpose:** Lists every defined notification category with label, description, and enabled state; the user toggles each category and saves via full-replacement update; changes apply to notifications generated after the save.
**Permission gate:** Authenticated session (TD §17 — DRF `IsAuthenticated` default; anonymous → 401)
**Feature source:** US-F022-004, FR-F022-008, FR-F022-009, AC-F022-006

