## 4. Navigation Changes

| Entry | Type | Target | Location | Condition |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Notification indicator (unread count) | New | /notifications | Application header (new AppHeader surface present on all routes) | Identified (authenticated) user |
| Notification preferences link | New | /notifications/preferences | Notification Center page | Always visible on the page |

## 5. Page Flow

Ordered sequence of user navigation through feature pages.

```
1. / → AppLayout renders the header; indicator hidden for anonymous; identified user sees unread count
2. Click notification indicator → /notifications (Notification Center, P-F022-002)
3. Mark single notification read → stays on page; indicator count updates from mutation response
4. Mark all as read → stays on page; indicator count → 0
5. Click "Notification preferences" → /notifications/preferences (P-F022-003)
6. Toggle categories and save → stays on page; save confirmation shown
7. Navigate back to /notifications or /
```

## 6. UI Behaviour Matrix

Bridges every user-facing Feature Specification requirement to implementation.

| # | User Action | Trigger | Backend (TD ref) | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | View unread count at a glance | Header renders; poll interval fires | API-F022-004: GET unread-count | NotificationIndicator shows the current count |
| 2 | Open Notification Center | Click notification indicator | Navigation → API-F022-001 | Browser navigates to /notifications; list query starts |
| 3 | View notification list | Navigate to /notifications | API-F022-001: GET list | NotificationCenterPage renders notifications newest first with title, message, timestamp, read state |
| 4 | Page through history | Click next/previous page control | API-F022-001: GET list?page=N | List renders the next/previous page of notifications |
| 5 | Mark single notification read | Click per-row mark-as-read | API-F022-002: POST /{id}/read/ | Row displays as read; indicator count updates from the authoritative response count |
| 6 | Mark all notifications read | Click mark-all-as-read | API-F022-003: POST /read-all/ | All rows display as read; indicator count → 0 |
| 7 | View preferences | Navigate to /notifications/preferences | API-F022-005: GET preferences | Preferences page lists all defined categories with enabled state |
| 8 | Change and save preferences | Toggle categories; click Save | API-F022-006: PUT preferences | Save confirmation; future generation gated server-side per FR-F022-009 |
| 9 | See new notifications without reload | Poll interval fires while any page is open | API-F022-004: GET unread-count | Indicator count refreshes; list query refreshes on invalidation/refetch |
| 10 | Indicator reflects read actions immediately | Any read mutation completes | API-F022-002 / API-F022-003 responses | Indicator updates from authoritative post-mutation counts |
| 11 | Anonymous user has no notification surface | Anonymous session on any route | TD §17 (IsAuthenticated) | Indicator hidden; notification routes redirect away |

**Traceability:** Rows 1–10 map to FR-F022-001 through FR-F022-011 and AC-F022-001 through AC-F022-008. Row 11 maps to FR-F022-010 / AC-F022-007 and TD §17. No user-facing requirement is left unmapped.

