## 10. Component Catalog

### C-F022-001 — NotificationIndicator
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-001 (surface present on all routes)
**Responsibility:** Displays the identified user's current unread notification count in the header; consumes the polled unread-count query; reflects authoritative counts from read-mutation responses; navigates to /notifications; hidden for anonymous users; degrades to no count after sustained poll failure.
**APIs consumed:** API-F022-004 (via C-F022-007)
**Permission gate:** Authenticated session (inherited from C-F022-008)
**State:** unreadCount (data owned by C-F022-007; rendered here)
**Requires empty/error handling:** Y

### C-F022-002 — NotificationCenterPage
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-002
**Responsibility:** Page container for the Notification Center; fetches the paginated notification list; owns the pagination cursor; triggers mark-all-as-read; provides the link to Notification Preferences; renders loading, empty, and error states.
**APIs consumed:** API-F022-001, API-F022-003 (via C-F022-007)
**Permission gate:** Authenticated session (route level)
**State:** currentPage; list data (data owned by C-F022-007; page cursor owned here)
**Requires empty/error handling:** Y

### C-F022-003 — NotificationList
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-002
**Responsibility:** Renders the paginated list of notifications newest first; delegates each entry to NotificationRow; renders the empty state.
**APIs consumed:** (none — receives data from parent)
**Permission gate:** (none — inherits from parent)
**State:** (none — stateless, receives props)
**Requires empty/error handling:** Y

### C-F022-004 — NotificationRow
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-002
**Responsibility:** Renders a single notification (title, message, timestamp, read state); triggers the mark-as-read mutation for its notification.
**APIs consumed:** API-F022-002 (via C-F022-007)
**Permission gate:** (none — inherits from parent)
**State:** (none — stateless, receives props)
**Requires empty/error handling:** N

### C-F022-005 — NotificationPreferencesPage
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-003
**Responsibility:** Page container for preferences; fetches the defined categories with enabled state; renders the form; handles loading and error states.
**APIs consumed:** API-F022-005 (via C-F022-007)
**Permission gate:** Authenticated session (route level)
**State:** preferences data (owned by C-F022-007; rendered here)
**Requires empty/error handling:** Y

### C-F022-006 — NotificationPreferencesForm
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-003
**Responsibility:** Renders one toggle per defined category; owns draft toggle state and save status; saves via full-replacement update; shows save success and error feedback.
**APIs consumed:** API-F022-006 (via C-F022-007)
**Permission gate:** (none — inherits from parent)
**State:** draftToggles; saveStatus
**Requires empty/error handling:** Y

### C-F022-007 — NotificationSyncService
**Type:** New
**Page:** All (app-level client data layer)
**Responsibility:** Single client data layer for the notification domain; owns the unread-count query (polled), the list query, and the preferences query; owns the mark-read, mark-all-read, and save-preferences mutations; owns the invalidation map so every mutation refreshes count and list; propagates typed loading/error/stale states to consuming surfaces.
**APIs consumed:** API-F022-001, API-F022-002, API-F022-003, API-F022-004, API-F022-005, API-F022-006 (all six, via the existing apiClient service)
**Permission gate:** (none — inherits from platform session; existing apiClient handles 401)
**State:** Query/mutation cache for unread count, notification list, and preferences
**Requires empty/error handling:** N (propagates typed states; not a rendering component)

### C-F022-008 — AppHeader
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-001 (surface present on all routes)
**Responsibility:** Application header surface; hosts the notification indicator; owns the identified-user gate derived from the existing session service; must never block page rendering when notification state is unavailable.
**APIs consumed:** (none directly — session via existing authService; indicator child consumes API-F022-004)
**Permission gate:** Authenticated session (component level)
**State:** identifiedUser (session state, derived from existing authService session check)
**Requires empty/error handling:** N

### C-F022-009 — AppLayout
**Type:** New
**Page:** P-F022-001, P-F022-002, P-F022-003 (app-level)
**Responsibility:** Application layout shell; owns the page structure — the header region (AppHeader) and the content region that renders the routed page.
**APIs consumed:** (none)
**Permission gate:** (none)
**State:** (none — stateless structure)
**Requires empty/error handling:** N

### AppRouteShell
**Type:** Modified
**Page:** All
**Responsibility:** Registers the application route set; wraps all routes in AppLayout; existing `/` route content remains unchanged.
**APIs consumed:** (none)
**Permission gate:** (none)
**State:** (none)
**Reuse rationale:** Existing application route shell (verified single `/` route); gains the new notification routes and layout composition.
**Requires empty/error handling:** N

## 11. API-to-Component Mapping

| API (TD §11) | Component | Method | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| API-F022-001 — List notifications | C-F022-007 (surfaced by C-F022-002 → C-F022-003) | GET | Fetch paginated notification list for the Notification Center |
| API-F022-002 — Mark single read | C-F022-007 (triggered by C-F022-004) | POST | Mark one notification read; response carries the authoritative unread count |
| API-F022-003 — Mark all read | C-F022-007 (triggered by C-F022-002) | POST | Mark all notifications read; response carries the authoritative unread count |
| API-F022-004 — Unread count | C-F022-007 (surfaced by C-F022-001) | GET | Polled unread-count endpoint for the header indicator |
| API-F022-005 — Get preferences | C-F022-007 (surfaced by C-F022-005) | GET | Fetch all defined categories with enabled state |
| API-F022-006 — Update preferences | C-F022-007 (triggered by C-F022-006) | PUT | Save full-replacement preferences |

## 12. Permission Mapping

The Technical Design does not define named fine-grained permissions. Section 17 (Security and Privacy) requires an authenticated session on every notification endpoint (DRF `IsAuthenticated` default; anonymous → 401). This is the single user-facing permission gate for F-022.

| Permission (TD §17) | Gate Location | Mechanism | Deny Behaviour |
|---|---|---|---|
| Authenticated session | Routes /notifications, /notifications/preferences | Route guard | Anonymous users redirected away from notification routes |
| Authenticated session | C-F022-008 (AppHeader) / C-F022-001 (NotificationIndicator) | Conditional render | Indicator hidden for anonymous users; header remains non-blocking |
| Authenticated session | C-F022-002..006 (notification pages) | Inherited route-level guard | Anonymous users never reach notification pages |

## 13. State Ownership

| State | Conceptual Owner | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| unreadCount | C-F022-007 (NotificationSyncService) | Polled query from API-F022-004; authoritative post-mutation counts from API-F022-002/003; rendered by C-F022-001 |
| notificationList (current page) | C-F022-007 (NotificationSyncService) | Query from API-F022-001; invalidated by read mutations; rendered by C-F022-002/003 |
| currentPage (pagination cursor) | C-F022-002 (NotificationCenterPage) | Page-local navigation state; passed to the list query |
| preferences (saved state) | C-F022-007 (NotificationSyncService) | Query from API-F022-005; updated by the API-F022-006 response |
| draftToggles / saveStatus | C-F022-006 (NotificationPreferencesForm) | Form-local draft state; server remains authoritative until save succeeds |
| identifiedUser (session) | C-F022-008 (AppHeader) | Derived from the existing authService session check; gates indicator visibility |

## 14. Reuse Opportunities

### Reused Without Change

| Candidate | Location | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| apiClient | Existing API client service module | Existing axios instance with `/api/` base, CSRF header injection, and 401 handling; consumed by C-F022-007 for all notification requests |
| authService (session check, User identity) | Existing auth service module | Existing session-state access reused for identified-user gating in C-F022-008 |
| theme | Existing MUI theme module | Existing theme consumed by new surfaces |
| React Query provider | Existing app-level provider in the entry module | Existing QueryClientProvider capability consumed by C-F022-007 |

### Modified

| Candidate | Location | Modification |
|---|---|---|
| AppRouteShell (application route shell) | Existing application route shell | Register new routes; wrap routes in AppLayout |

### Not Reused

| Candidate | Location | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| SystemInfo | Existing components directory | Bootstrapped pipeline-validation placeholder that fetches system status; no structural relationship to the notification domain; raw-fetch pattern with local state, incompatible with the shared sync-service model |
| authService-as-flat-function-module pattern | Existing auth service module | Auth-scoped module; adding notification queries/mutations would pollute its boundary and provide no shared cache, invalidation map, or polling |
| MUI library primitives (e.g., AppBar, Badge, List) | Third-party UI library (existing dependency) | Library primitives, not application components; they are building blocks composed inside new components, not reusable application surfaces |

### New Components — Justification

| Component | Why New | Candidates Evaluated |
|---|---|---|
| C-F022-001 (NotificationIndicator) | No header or indicator surface exists in the application (verified) | SystemInfo — unrelated; MUI primitives — library baseline only |
| C-F022-002 (NotificationCenterPage) | No page component exists beyond the inline root content (verified) | SystemInfo — unrelated |
| C-F022-003 (NotificationList) | No list component exists (verified) | MUI List — library primitive, no domain behavior |
| C-F022-004 (NotificationRow) | No row/item component exists (verified) | MUI ListItem — library primitive, no domain behavior |
| C-F022-005 (NotificationPreferencesPage) | No preferences/settings surface exists (verified) | authService — no UI; SystemInfo — unrelated |
| C-F022-006 (NotificationPreferencesForm) | No form/settings component exists (verified) | MUI form primitives — library baseline only |
| C-F022-007 (NotificationSyncService) | No client data layer for the notification domain exists; existing services are auth-scoped function modules | authService pattern — rejected (pollutes auth boundary; no shared cache/invalidation/polling) |
| C-F022-008 (AppHeader) | No application header surface exists (verified: the route shell renders inline content only) | SystemInfo — unrelated; MUI AppBar — library primitive |
| C-F022-009 (AppLayout) | No layout or page-shell component exists (verified) | App route shell — minimal, has no layout responsibility |

## 15. Frontend Design Decisions

### FD-F022-001 — F-022 introduces the application header surface
**Context:** FR-F022-004 requires a header notification indicator, and the success measures require reaching the Notification Center from the header. Codebase inspection confirms no header or layout component exists; the application route shell renders inline content only.
**Selected approach:** Create a new AppHeader surface hosting the notification indicator, contained in a new AppLayout shell that wraps all routes, making the indicator platform-wide.
**Alternatives considered:** (a) Embed the indicator only on notification routes — rejected: the indicator must be visible from the general surface per US-F022-001; (b) defer header creation to another feature — rejected: no other feature provides a header, and F-022 requires the surface.
**Rationale:** The header is a structural prerequisite for the feature's core "at a glance" behaviour; the minimal layout wraps the existing route set without altering page content.
**Consequences:** Every existing and future route renders inside AppLayout; AppHeader must remain non-blocking when notification state is unavailable.
**TD dependency:** CMP-F022-004 (Header Notification Indicator), API-F022-004.

### FD-F022-002 — Notification preferences as a dedicated page
**Context:** TD CMP-F022-005 allows a "page or section" for preferences; no settings page exists in the frontend.
**Selected approach:** Standalone route /notifications/preferences.
**Alternatives considered:** (a) Section within the Notification Center page — rejected: mixes list operations with configuration concerns and couples the preference flow to list navigation; (b) new general settings page — rejected: invents a broader surface beyond F-022 scope.
**Rationale:** A dedicated page keeps the preferences surface reachable, focused, and independent of list state; it matches the approved "preferences section" scope without expanding into a settings feature.
**Consequences:** One additional route; the Notification Center links to it.
**TD dependency:** CMP-F022-005 (Notification Preferences Surface), API-F022-005, API-F022-006.

### FD-F022-003 — NotificationSyncService as the single client data layer
**Context:** TD CMP-F022-006 requires a client sync service owning queries, mutations, invalidation, and polling. The codebase has no such layer; the only existing data access is the auth service module and a raw-fetch placeholder.
**Selected approach:** New NotificationSyncService consumes the existing apiClient, owns all notification queries/mutations and the invalidation map; all three surfaces consume notification data through it.
**Alternatives considered:** (a) Extend the auth service module with notification functions — rejected: pollutes the auth-scoped module boundary and provides no shared cache, invalidation, or polling; (b) per-component direct API calls — rejected: inconsistent count/list sync and duplication.
**Rationale:** Centralizing notification data access makes the three surfaces consistent (TD CMP-F022-006) and reuses the existing apiClient rather than introducing a second HTTP layer.
**Consequences:** C-F022-001/002/004/005/006 consume via C-F022-007; the invalidation map keeps the indicator and list converged.
**TD dependency:** CMP-F022-006 (Client Notification Sync Service), API-F022-001..006.

### FD-F022-004 — Identified-user gating reuses the existing session check
**Context:** Notification endpoints require an authenticated session (TD §17); the indicator and notification routes must be invisible to anonymous users (FR-F022-010, AC-F022-007). The frontend already exposes session state through the existing auth service session check.
**Selected approach:** AppHeader owns the identified-user gate derived from the existing session check; anonymous users see no indicator and are redirected away from notification routes.
**Alternatives considered:** (a) Assume a session is present — rejected: would surface the indicator to anonymous users; (b) introduce a new auth state store — rejected: no store is needed for this scope; the existing session service suffices.
**Rationale:** Reuse-first: the platform's session capability already exists and is the honest evidence for gating; no new auth architecture is required.
**Consequences:** Indicator visibility is tied to session state; the header remains non-blocking regardless.
**TD dependency:** TD §17 (IsAuthenticated), CMP-F022-004.

### FD-F022-005 — Server-side pagination for the Notification Center
**Context:** The list endpoint is paginated server-side (API-F022-001, DRF PageNumberPagination, PAGE_SIZE 25; EAF-F022-002) with deterministic ordering.
**Selected approach:** The Notification Center uses the server-provided page-based pagination; the page cursor is owned by the Notification Center page and passed to the list query.
**Alternatives considered:** (a) Infinite scroll — rejected: the API returns paginated pages, not a continuous stream; (b) client-side paging of a full list — rejected: would require transferring full histories, violating the design's transfer bounds.
**Rationale:** The backend contract defines page semantics; the frontend adopts them directly, keeping transfers bounded and ordering deterministic.
**Consequences:** The list query is page-parameterized; the page cursor is page-local state.
**TD dependency:** API-F022-001 (pagination), EAF-F022-002.

## 16. Ready for Review

- [x] Every user-facing Feature Specification requirement traces to a page or component
- [x] UI Behaviour Matrix covers every user-facing requirement and acceptance criterion
- [x] Every user-facing API from Technical Design §11 is mapped to at least one component
- [x] Every user-facing permission from Technical Design §17 is gated on a page, route, or component
